    "narrative": "Our lineup for 2026-06-20 leans heavily into speed and opportunistic matchups, headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (68.37). **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, bolstered by a massive +16% SP skill adjustment against Walbert Ure\u00f1a and a +10% park factor that elevates him above his baseline. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Rea, leveraging a +13% SP skill bump that makes him an elite start despite the modest SB hold threat. **Bryson Stott** (63.12) is another critical piece today; while his raw projections are tempered by the lineup order, he gains a +13% platoon edge and, crucially, a +4% boost due to the slow delivery of Freddy Peralta, which should provide a runway for our high-priority SB category.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly rigorous today, with **Drew Gilbert** (39.49) narrowly missing the cut by falling just below our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. While **Drew Gilbert** projects well as a depth piece, the lack of an optimal lineup spot\u2014pushed down to the 8-hole\u2014stripped away the necessary points to justify a start over more central options like **Jonathan Aranda** (56.90). We are tracking significant risks with **Taylor Ward** (46.10), who faces a tough assignment against Yoshinobu Yamamoto. While the wind-out factor provides a small +5% cushion, his -17% SP skill adjustment and poor platoon leverage make him a volatile play we\u2019ll need to monitor closely. Additionally, with **Cal Raleigh**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Taylor Ward** all awaiting official lineup confirmation, we are keeping a close eye on any late-inning pivots that could jeopardize our projected order-based bonuses.",
